; Network-effect boundary for one explicitly selected C# declaration.
;
; This is the shipped specialization. Its ship-time declaration selection is
; the empty set, so a repository that enables this policy without editing the
; selection block below carries no purity obligation at all. Purity is never
; inferred from a method name, a class name, a namespace prefix, a file name, a
; comment, or an attribute.
;
; Activation
; ----------
; 1. Ship or install the reviewed C# semantic model that declares the concrete
;    .NET network API identity with the effect `bifrost.network_io`.
;    `semantic-packs/web-network/csharp/bifrost.web-network-csharp.json` is that
;    reviewed model. Place it under `.bifrost/semantic-models/`. It is a `csharp`
;    / `dotnet` model, which is the evidence row every .NET workspace publishes
;    for its shared-framework reference assemblies, so a workspace that already
;    resolves its dependencies activates it without further configuration.
; 2. Replace both declaration selections in the analysis block below with the
;    exact declaration(s) this repository protects, for example:
;      (language csharp
;        (enclosing-decl
;          (inside-decl (class :name "PriceCalculator")
;            (method :name "Total"))))
; 3. Enable the policy: `bifrost --policy-id
;    bifrost.effects.csharp.selected-boundary-no-network-io --fail-on error`.
;
; Why this API
; ------------
; The reviewed identity is `System.Net.Http.HttpClient.SendAsync` at its
; written arity one. That is a receiver route: `SendAsync` is an instance
; method, so the C# resolver must first resolve the receiver's declared type
; through that file's own `using` tiers and the external declaration surface
; before the identity exists at all. The written arity one is part of the
; identity, so it is unambiguous against the `(request, cancellationToken)`,
; `(request, completionOption)` and three-argument overloads. `HttpClient.GetAsync`
; would bind the same way but takes a bare string or `Uri`, which makes the
; call shape easier to imitate accidentally; `SendAsync(HttpRequestMessage)` is
; the request-object form the reviewed model declares.
;
; The route is async. An awaited call reaches the declared effect in the same
; invocation and is reported as a declared effect with its witness chain. A
; call handed to a callback or a scheduler the analyzer cannot expand is not
; reported as an effect and is not reported as clean either: the coverage stays
; open and the run publishes an unmet obligation.
;
; The rule body is shared across languages; only the language label, the
; activated model, and this selection block differ.
;
; The join
; --------
; `procedure-effects` projects one row per (procedure, effect id) with the
; classification (direct or transitive), certainty, timing, coverage and a
; bounded witness chain. Rows are keyed on the declaration domain's own
; `procedure_id`, so the join to the selected relation is declaration-identity
; equality.
;
; The absence claim
; -----------------
; `(exactly 0)` is an absence claim, so it is conclusive only when the effect
; relation's coverage is exhaustive. A selected declaration that reaches an
; unresolved helper leaves the effect set open; the run then publishes an unmet
; obligation instead of reporting a clean verdict, and a helper chain the
; analyzer cannot expand is never reported as an absence.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.effects.csharp.selected-boundary-no-network-io"
  :name "Selected C# boundary reaches no network effect"
  :message "the selected C# boundary reaches the declared network effect"
  :severity error
  :description "One explicitly selected C# declaration must not reach a declared network effect, directly or through workspace helpers. The effect is declared by the reviewed C# semantic model on the exact .NET API identity, never inferred from a method name, a class name, a namespace prefix, a file name, a comment, or an attribute. The ship-time selection is empty; configure the declaration-selection block before enabling this policy."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#network-effect-boundary"
  :tags ["effects" "network" "boundary" "csharp"]
  :analysis
    (analysis
      :type assertion
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      ; Declaration-selection block. Ship-time selection: the empty set.
      ; Replace both `(except ...)` expressions below with the exact
      ; declaration this repository protects. The `effect` binding repeats the
      ; same selection on purpose: `procedure-effects` derives a closure for
      ; every declaration its input query returns, so repeating the selection
      ; is what keeps the policy from deriving effects for declarations it did
      ; not select. With the ship-time empty selection it derives none, the
      ; assertion has no group to judge, and the run is vacuously clean.
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      (bind :name selected
        :query (rql :schema-version 1
          (language csharp
            (except
              (enclosing-decl (method))
              (enclosing-decl (method))))))
      (bind :name effect
        :query (rql :schema-version 1
          (language csharp
            (procedure-effects
              (except
                (enclosing-decl (method))
                (enclosing-decl (method)))))))
      (join :left selected :right effect :on ((id procedure_id)))
      (group :name selected-boundary :by (selected.id)
        (aggregate :name network-effects :op count
          :where ((effect.effect_id eq "bifrost.network_io")
                  (effect.derivation eq declared))))
      (assert :group selected-boundary :value network-effects :cardinality (exactly 0))))
